Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 AUG 96 ACCESSIONED ON  19 AUG 96 at 10 43 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 3  EXTENSIVELY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR INFERIOR MARGIN OF SPECIMEN AND TO ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR SUPERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS AND EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR SUPERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL INFEROMEDIAL MARGIN  1    ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL INFEROMEDIAL MARGIN  2    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN TWO OF FOURTEEN LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL LYMPH NODES    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN FIVE OF FIVE LYMPH NODES  NOTE  The tumor in the lymph nodes does not transgress the lymph node capsules  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 AUG 96 at 15 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in five parts  Labeled with the patient s name and number  Labeled  right breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm piece of breast with a short and long suture and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE tan to red  ill defined  firm mass which extends close to the superior anterior margin  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and now submitted in cassette A  The specimen is inked in black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm tan to red  ill defined firm mass that extends close to the anterior inferior and anterior superior margin  Representative portions of the lesion are submitted as follows  Section code  A  Frozen section  B  Anterior inferior margin  C  Anterior superior margin  D G  Representative portions of mass  Part 2 is received fresh in a single container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and number and further labeled   1  Additional inframedial margin   The specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of breast tissue that is inked entirely in black and additionally in yellow over the half on which a lung suture is attached  The specimen is sectioned to reveal multiple cysts  the largest measuring 6mm in diameter  Representative portions are submitted starting at the short suture in casette H and progressing throughout the lesion into cassette K  Part 3 is received fresh in a single container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and number and further labeled  2 additional inframedial margin  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue with long and short suture attached  The specimen is sectioned to reveal in the half farther away from the short suture  a yellow fatty area closer to the long suture laying on top of a tan fibrous area further away from the long suture  This distinction diminishes in the specimen progressing towards the short suture  Representative sections are submitted progressing from the short suture throughout the specimen  in cassettes L   M  Received fresh in the container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and number and further labeled  right axillary tissue contents  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue that is dissected and submitted in cassettes N P  Part 4  received fresh in a single container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and number and further labeled  additional axillary tissue  consists of three fragments of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in aggregate  The specimen is dissected  lymph nodes are identified and submitted in cassettes R   Q  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT  SUPERIOR ANTERIOR MARGIN   INVASIVE CARCINOMA EXTENDING CLOSE TO THE MARGIN  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY PART B  RIGHT BREAST   ADDITIONAL INFEROMEDIAL MARGIN  1  PART C  RIGHT BREAST   ADDITIONAL INFEROMEDIAL MARGIN  2  PART D  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART E  ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES , Positive.
