rgin  radial section  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast additional subareolar tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal a 80  yellow lobulated fatty to 20  dense white fibrous tissue surface  The specimen is entirely submitted as N P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm aggregate of adipose tissue which contains multiple tan red rubbery to focally firm lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 8cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Q  Two lymph nodes R  A whole lymph nodes S  Two whole lymph nodes T W  One bisected lymph node in each X  One trisected lymph node Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shave margin superior cavity right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal a 70  yellow lobulated to 30  dense white fibrous tissue surface  The specimen is entirely submitted as Y DD  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lateral half of cavity final shave margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal a 70  yellow lobulated fatty to 30  dense white fibrous tissue surface  The specimen is entirely submitted as EE HH  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  SMN                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT ADDITIONAL SUBAREOLAR TISSUE   EXCIS PART C  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY   EXCISI