Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  LUMPECTOMY  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LEE  KENNETH  ROBERT  M D   DIAGNOSIS  by LEE KENNETH ROBERT M D   SPECIMEN LABELED  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE    Residual well differentiated mucinous  colloid  carcinoma adjacent to  previous biopsy cavity  slides 5 7    Multiple foci of atypical ductal hyperplasia and ductal carcinoma in  situ  cribriform type  with a single focus of DCIS less than 1mm from  deep resection margin  section  9    Proliferative fibrocystic change   Case reviewed by Dr  Susan Lester who concurs   SPECIMEN LABELED  SCAR    Skin with suture reaction   No carcinoma   SURGICAL ADDENDUM  by LEE KENNETH ROBERT M D   The following information supplements that given in the original diagnosis   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU is present in four of the nine blocks from the right  breast re excision  blocks 6 through 9   In three of these blocks the  carcinoma in situ is at or within 0 2cm of the margin  Because the specimen  was received in two fragments and was unoriented  the location of these margins  within the breast cannot be determined  The carcinoma in situ is in the  general vicinity of the biopsy cavity  but is not within the biopsy cavity  itself   The carcinoma in situ has a variety of histologic appearances ranging from  large epithelioid cells with a cribriform architecture to focally smaller less  cohesive cells resembling lobular carcinoma in situ  There are also numerous  areas in which the cells take on a spindled morphology with small rosette like  cribriform spaces  Focal calcification is associated with some of the  cribriform spaces  There are numerous areas of atypical hyperplasia also with  this spindle cell morphology  some bordering on a diagnosis of carcinoma in  situ  blocks 2 and 3    The residual invasive colloid carcinoma measures less than 0 2cm   CLINICAL DATA   History  S p right breast biopsy 2 weeks ago  path   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   reported as  mucinous  colloid  carcinoma well differentiated margin   no free    Patient underwent today additional excision biopsy of the area of  previous biopsy    Operation  Re excision right breast cancer   Clinical Diagnosis  Pre Op  Breast cancer   Post Op  Pending path   TISSUE SUBMITTED   1  Right breast tissue    2  Ssar   GROSS DESCRIPTION  by DRY SARAH MARGARET M D   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  medical record number and   1   right breast tissue   are two fragments of fibrofatty breast tissue  4 9 x REMOVED_DATE  x 0 8cm in aggregate   The larger specimen  3 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm   containing  three stitches surrounding a central cavity  1 x 1 2cm    The opposite side of  the specimen is smooth and glistening white and grossly it is consistent with  the deep margin  NOTE  This specimen arrives unoriented  The presumed deep  margin is inked in black  the surface containing the incision is inked in red  and incision cavity itself is inked in green  Serial sectioning through the  specimen does not reveal any lesions grossly suspicious for residual  carcinoma   MICRO  1  Smaller fragment  1 frag  ESS   MICRO  2 9  Right breast tissue  larger fragment  mult frags  ESS   Specimen  2  received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  medical record  number  and   2  scar   is a specimen  2 9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm in overall  dimensions  consisting of an ellipse of skin  3 2 x 0 5cm   with a central  incision  1 8cm in length  and two attached surgical surgical sutures  NOTE   The specimen arrives unoriented  The external resection margins are inked in  black and the margin of the central margin are inked in red  There is no gross  evidence of invasive carcinoma in the specimen  The specimen is serially  sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  10 and 11   MICRO  10 and 11  Scar  mult frags  mult frags  ESS   Reports to  GOLDSTEIN  DONALD  PETER M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  LUMPECTO