lightly outer breast posteriorly  Suspicious  retropectoral lymph nodes were seen and several right axillary lymph  nodes appeared enlarged  There was no enhancement of the underlying  pectoralis muscle  or evidence of involvement of the skin  A fine  needle aspiration of a right axillary node was positive for metastatic  carcinoma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     The patient was treated with neoadjuvant chemotherapy using Taxotere   carboplatin and Herceptin  She had a complete clinical and  radiological response   Grossly  no area in the mastectomy specimen was suspicious for invasive  carcinoma  Two clips marking the prior core needle biopsy sites were  identified  The tissue around the clips shows stromal fibrosis and DCIS  consistent with the tumor bed  No residual invasive carcinoma is  seen   The residual DCIS is similar in nuclear grade to the pretreatment DCIS   However  the cells are present as a single layer and do not fill the  ducts   The lymph nodes are free of carcinoma  No fibrous scarring is present   The patient has had a pathologic complete response to treatment and  would be classified as Miller Payne response score of 5 and Residual  Cancer Burden  RCB  class 0   This carcinoma would be classified as AJCC  6th edition  y Tis  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    CLINICAL DATA   History  49 year old female with locally advanced right breast cancer  s p  neoadjuvant chemotherapy  Complete clinical and imaging response   Operation  Left breast simple mastectomy and right breast modified radical  mastectomy   Operative Findings  Not provided   Clinical Diagnosis  Left breast   high risk of cancer and right breast cancer   s p neoadjuvant therapy   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Left breast simple mastectomy  short suture superior  long  suture superior   B 2  Right breast simple mastectomy  short suture superior  long  suture lateral   C 3  Right axillary contents  Levels I and II   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh  in three parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATI