Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  06 AUG 98 at 12 22 CLINICAL DATA  Nodularity  left upper outer quadrant with atypia on FNA  On hormone replacement                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  MASS    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIAMETER AND EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   BREAST  LEFT  MASS  2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA SPANNING AT LEAST 1CM IN GREATEST DIAMETER AND EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  RADIAL SCAR  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels and blood vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 16 25 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 AUG 98 at 14 14     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for HER 2  Favorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   1   left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a 2 0cm in greatest dimension  irregular  firm area  A representative section of the firm area is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in Cassette A  The remaining tissue is entirely submitted in Cassettes B D  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   2   left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and bisected to reveal a white  fibrous cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted in Cassette E  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  CONSISTENT WITH LOBULAR ORIGIN EXTENDING TO INKED MARGIN  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  2  NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Barbara