Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  DORFMAN  DAVID  MICHAEL  M D  PH D   DIAGNOSIS  by DORFMAN DAVID MICHAEL M D  PH D   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE  BIOPSY   INVOLVEMENT BY NON HODGKIN S LYMPHOMA  DIFFUSE  LARGE CELL TYPE   B CELL PHENOTYPE  Sections show breast parenchyma and fibroadipose tissue diffusely  infiltrated by an atypical lymphoid infiltrate comprised of intermediate  sized to large cells with distinct nucleoli  round to ovoid nuclei  and  a moderate amount of cytoplasm  Scattered eosinophils and histiocytes  are seen  Frequent mitoses and apoptotic bodies are noted   Immunoperoxidase studies performed at BWH on paraffin sections reveal  the large atypical cells to be reactive for the B cell marker  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    These cells co express bcl 2  but are negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Staining for  kappa and lambda light chains are difficult to interpret due to high  background staining   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  highlights scattered T cells and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   highlights scattered follicular dendritic cells  The Ki 67  MIB 1   stain highlights approximately 80  of cells   NOTE   The histologic and immunophenotypic studies are consistent with  involvement by a NON HODGKIN S LYMPHOMA  DIFFUSE  LARGE CELL TYPE   B CELL PHENOTYPE   CLINICAL DATA   History  74 year old female with right breast mass  28mm in subareolar region   History of non Hodgkin s lymphoma diagnosed after right breast skin lesion  biopsied  Treated with CHOP  no xrt    Operation  R breast biopsy   TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  Right breast tissue  short superior  long lateral  whip  deep margin    GROSS DESCRIPTION  by LEE BENJAMIN H  M D  PH D   The specimen is received fresh and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  medical  record number and  right breast tissue   The specimen consists of breast  biopsy specimen weighing 11 grams and measuring 4cm from medial to lateral  3  cm from inferior to superior  1 5cm from posterior to anterior  The specimen  is received oriented with two stitches as per surgeon   long stitch is lateral  and short stitch is superior  The specimen is also inked by the surgeon per  pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior   black  anterior    blue  superior   red  inferior   green  lateral   yellow  medial   orange   After sectioning  three areas of firmness are identified  the largest of which  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  This is also the most medial area of firmness   It lies 0 1cm from the anterior margin  0 5cm from the posterior margin and  0 3cm from the inferior margin  The second area is 0 5cm lateral to the  first one and is located 0 5cm from the anterior margin  0 2cm from the  posterior margin and 0 1cm from the inferior margin  The third area is 0 3cm  away from the second one and is 0 2cm from the posterior margin  0 4cm from  the anterior margin and 0 1cm from the inferior margin  The entire specimen  is submitted for histologic evaluation   Micro REMOVED_DATE  right breast biopsy specimen submitted from medial to lateral  the  areas described are present in cassettes 3  5   7   Reports to  RHEI  ESTHER M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS   report_end  , Positive.
