Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  11 AUG 98 at 14 21 CLINICAL DATA  Palpable mass  abnormal mammogram  Positive FNA  Blue dye only mapping                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  SINGLE FOCUS SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM AND PRESENT AT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels and blood vessels is not seen  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  IN THE REGION OF THE MASS  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN SEVEN OF SEVEN LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  BREAST   RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN THREE OF THREE LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  14 AUG 98 at 18 11 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 AUG 98 at 09 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  short   superior  long   lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  which has been infused with blue dye  The specimen is entirely inked black  with the posterior margin over inked in blue  and the superior margin over inked in yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral and reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm firm  tan mass  which abuts the posterior margin  which is covered with a thin fascia  pectoralis majora   The mass is 1 7cm from the superior margin  1 3cm from the inferior margin  and 1 0cm from the anterior margin  A representative section of the mass is frozen as FX 1 and is saved frozen  SECTION CODE  A B  Tumor to closest posterior margin  C   Tumor to closest inferior margin  D   Tumor to closest anterior margin  E   Tumor to closest superior margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of adipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  A representative s