n no acute distress     The right breast showed a 1 5cm tender  ovoid and rubbery nodule     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation     3 aspirates was were performed using 25 gauge needles with local anesthesia and  without complications   3 slides were stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by  Rosemary Tambouret  M D and David Hwang  M D     Disposition  The immediate interpretation was not discussed with the patient   Kevin Hughes  M D   was notified of the preliminary results by personal  communication at 3 30 P M         The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Rosemary H Tambouret MD on REMOVED_DATE 16 43       CLINICAL HISTORY  Self discovered right breast mass at about REMOVED_DATE 00  clinically  Dr  Hughes  suspects of fibroadenoma        SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT  Received 3 slides in ETOH  Received 3 air dried  slides  Received 3cc s of pink fluid  One SurePath slide made           Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT       report_end  , Positive.
