m  is present   0 1cm from the new final  anterior margin  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     No in situ carcinoma is seen   Note  Some of the carcinoma may be present in lymphatic spaces   FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN   Benign breast tissue with no carcinoma seen   FINAL DEEP MARGIN   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  0 5cm  is present   No lymphovascular invasion is seen   No in situ carcinoma is seen   The new final deep margin is not oriented and can not be assessed   FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  is present as at least two foci 0 1cm and 0 2cm on  the glass slide   No lymphovascular invasion is seen   No in situ carcinoma is seen   The new final anterior margin is not oriented and can not be assessed   AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION   ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS are present in one  1  of twelve  12  axillary lymph nodes   approximately 50 cells   0 02cm    The tumor cells are not associated with a  fibrous scar  The remaining nodes do not show evidence of prior tumor  involvement   Note  The patient presented with a palpable mass  Imaging studies showed a 3  cm mass in the upper outer breast and a 1 5cm mass  3cm inferior and anterior  to the first mass  Numerous calcifications were present in the same region   There was an enlarged axillary lymph node   A core needle biopsy of the 3cm mass revealed a moderately differentiated  invasive ductal carcinoma  positive for ER and PR and negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu   1     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    A core needle biopsy performed at the same time for upper  outer calcifications did not remove the targeted calcifications and only showed  benign tissue  A fine needle aspiration of the enlarged lymph node showed  malignant cells consistent with breast cancer   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     The patient received neoadjuvant therapy  The 3cm mass decreased in size to 2  cm and the 1 5cm mass decreased in size to 1cm  The lymph node also became  smaller   The double wire localized excision removed the larger cancer marked by two  clips  Approximately half the cancer shows diminished cellularity  consistent  with a minimal response to treatment  The overall cellularity of the carcinoma  is estimated at 50   for a Miller Payne score of 2 and a Residual Cancer Burden  score of REMOVED_DATE  RCB II   The carcinoma appears to be have been transected  due to the presence of  carcinoma in three of the margins   The singe wire localized excision removed the calcifications in the  upper outer quadrant originally targeted by the prior core needle biopsy   No carcinoma is seen in this area   It is not clear that the 1 5cm mass was removed in this procedure  An  MRI after this surgery revealed a 1 9cm mass adjacent to the seroma cavity  suspicious for carcinoma  Clinical correlation is suggested   The single lymph node with metastatic carcinoma does not show evidence  of prior more extensive tumor involvement or evidence of the prior FNA   Although this could be consistent with a marked response of the metastatic  carcinoma to treatment  it is also possible that the lymph node with  metastatic carcinoma was not removed  It is unusual for metastatic  carcinoma to respond to a greater extent than the carcinoma in the breast   The post treatment MRI showed a 1cm mass in the axilla suspicious for a  lymph node  Clinical correlation is suggested to determine if the  previously involved lymph node was excised   The carcinoma would be classified as  at least  AJCC  6th edition    yp  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   i     CLINICAL DATA   History  Breast cancer  s p neoadjuvant therapy   TISSUE SUBMITTED   Consult slides   GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received from Massachusetts General Hospital  Fruit Street  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID    are sixty three H E stained glass slides labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and sublabeled    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   to   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   to   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   to   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_