Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Molecular Pathology Report  Translocation Assay for Lung Tumor      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  M   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  74   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  ELLISON 19  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 23 19  Results To   Michael Lanuti MD      CLINICAL HISTORY   Lung Adenocarcinoma    SPECIMENS RECEIVED   A  Molecular test for Translocation Assay for Lung    GROSS DESCRIPTION   1 block s   4 unstained slide s  from Massachusetts General Hospital    SLIDE BLOCK DESCRIPTION    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID             TEST   ALK  RET   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  NGS Gene Fusion Assay    INDICATION FOR TEST  Lung Adenocarcinoma    SPECIMEN S  TESTED   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA   United States     RESULTS   Targeted next generation sequencing  NGS  using Anchored Multiplex PCR  AMP   detected no fusion transcripts in the specified exons of the following genes   ALK  exons 19 22    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   exons 31 37   and RET  exons 8 13      INTERPRETATION     NEGATIVE for ALK  RET  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  rearrangement     TEST INFORMATION   We have developed a multiplex polymerase chain reaction  PCR  technology termed  Anchored Multiplex PCR  AMP  for fusion transcript detection using targeted next  generation sequencing  NGS   Briefly  total nucleic acid was isolated from a  formalin fixed paraffin embedded tumor specimen after histological review for  tumor enrichment  The total nucleic acid was reverse transcribed with random  hexamers  followed by second strand synthesis to create double stranded  complementary DNA  cDNA   The double stranded cDNA was end repaired   adenylated  and ligated with a half functional adapter  Two hemi nested PCR  reactions were applied to create a fully functional sequencing library that  targets ALK exons REMOVED_DATE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  exons REMOVED_DATE  RET exons REMOVED_DATE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  exon 2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   exon 6  and GAPDH exon 6  Illumina MiSeq 2 x 151 base pair paired end  sequencing results were aligned to the hg19 human genome reference using a  combination of bwa  1  and BLAT  2   A laboratory developed algorithm was used  for fusion transcript detection and annotation  The integrity of the input  nucleic acid and the technical performance of the assay were assessed with  control sequences from the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and GAPDH targets  Although this assay  may detect several potential fusion variants  only the most prevalent one is  reported  The assay is validated for samples showing 20  or higher tumor  cellularity     REFERENCES   1  Kent WJ  Genome Res  REMOVED_CASE_ID  12 4  656 64   PMID   REMOVED_CASE_ID    2  Li H and Durbin R  Bioinformatics  REMOVED_CASE_ID  25 14   REMOVED_CASE_ID  60   PMID   REMOVED_CASE_ID      This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Center for Integrated Diagnostics  It has not been cleared or approved  by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that such  clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical purposes   Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has established and  verified the test accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH Internal Address  Center for Integrated Diagnostics   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St  Jackson  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID           Electronically Signed Out By  Long Phi Le MD  PhD         PART   Molecular test for Translocation Ass