situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested NOTE  The lobular carcinoma cells stain for keratin 903 but do not stain for e cadherin  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13 10                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block T   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 26 Proofread by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm piece of tan red adipose tissue with a guide wire running through it  A bow tie stitch marks the superior margin  a long stitch marking the lateral margin  and a short stitch mark the anterior margin  Between the anterior and lateral stitch markings there is a skin ellipse that measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and contains no lesions  The entire specimen is inked anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow and sectioned along the medial lateral axis from medial to lateral to reveal yellow unremarkable appearing adipose tissue as well as white fibrous appearing tissue  with no obvious identifiable lesions visually  Upon palpation the specimen appears to be