 potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation     2 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles with local anesthesia and  without complications   2 slides were stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by  Amy Ly  M D     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were not discussed with the  patient  Michelle Specht  MD was notified of the preliminary results by text  message at 3 10 p m           The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation          Electronically Signed Out By  Amy Ly MD on REMOVED_DATE 11 18       CLINICAL HISTORY  Distant left breast DCIS  left breast nodule on surgical scar         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 1 slides in ETOH  Received 3 air dried  slides             Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT       report_end  , Positive.
