Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  18 MAY 93 at 12 37 CLINICAL DATA  Lesion  left breast  measuring approximately 3cm                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  COMPLEX SCLEROSING LESION  RADICAL SCAR   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The change in diagnosis from the frozen section interpretation is based on microscopic examination of the entire lesion  This case is unusual by virtue of its large size  Several pathologists have reviewed this case including Dr  Frederick Koerner  Dr  Ben Pilch  Dr  Robert Young and Dr  Robert Scully and all agree with this diagnosis  Diagnosis by  John O Connell  M D  Signed On  22 MAY 93 at 10 26                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   1   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    OTHER CASES OF COMPLEX SCLEROSING LESION HAVE NOT PREVIOUSLY BEEN EXAMINED BY THIS METHOD AND THEREFORE HISTORICAL DATA IS NOT AVAILABLE FOR COMPARISON  Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 93 at 16 47     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Estradiol receptor  Positive 26 femtomoles mg protein  Progestin receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire in place and an attached specimen x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm tan  firm  gritty  ill defined mass that grossly abuts the inked resection margin  The remainder of the specimen is composed of fibroadipose tissue with fibrous white bands  A representative piece is frozen as Frozen Sections  1 and  2 and saved frozen  Representative tissue is taken for estrogen receptors and BRDU studies  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in A through N  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SCIRRHOUS TYPE  O R  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Positive.
