esult was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 MAY 97 at 14 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section labelled with the patients name  unit number  and   left breast lesion  are two fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm of tan red and yellow fibroadipose tissue  the latter on a needle localization wire  The first fragment is quite firm  Both fragments are inked black and sectioned to reveal that the first fragment has a 0 2cm central red area  surrounded by tan yellow tissue  The first fragment is entirely submitted in A   C  and the second in D   F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  name and unit number  are three specimens  Labeled  number 1  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan   red fibrofatty tissue fragment  inked black  bisected  and entirely submitted in G   H  Labeled  number 2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm irregular tan   pink and yellow fibrofatty tissue fragment  inked black  bisected  and entirely submitted in I   J  Labeled  number 3  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan   pink and yellow fibrofatty tissue fragment  with a single stitch indicating the side furthest from tumor  inked black  The other side is inked red  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes K M  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PA