ual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of tissue with a rubbery 0 4cm nodule  The adjacent areas are somewhat irregular  Entirely submitted in cassettes A and B  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five more separate specimens  Labelled  A   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  inked  all submitted in cassette C  Labelled  B   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  inked and all submitted in cassette D  Labelled  C   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  inked and entirely submitted in cassette E  Labelled  D   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue inked and entirely submitted in cassette F  Labelled  E   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm piece of fibroadipose 