rcinoma  this carcinoma is unusual in that there is e cadherin  positivity  There is also weak membrane immunoreactivity for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  FISH  studies could be performed if clinically warranted   The CIS also has a predominantly  lobular  pattern  However  the nuclear grade  is slightly higher than typical and there are very focal areas with a  cribriform or microfollicular pattern  E cadherin is positive in the areas of  cribriforming and in the areas that have a more  lobular  appearance  The CIS  is restricted to the areas of invasive carcinoma and is not seen outside the  areas of invasive carcinoma   This carcinoma would be classified best as AJCC  6th edition   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    LEFT BREAST  SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN   INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  is present as multiple foci in four of eight  blocks  the largest focus measuring 0 8cm   No lymphovascular or perineural invasion are seen   CIS  solid type  is present as a minor component within the invasive carcinoma   Invasive carcinoma is present at the inferior margin over a broad front   Presumably this is adjacent to the main excision   Invasive carcinoma is 0 2cm from the superior margin   Invasive carcinoma is   0 1cm from the anterior and lateral margins  Clinical  correlation is necessary to determine if these are true surgical margins  The  remaining resection margins are free    0 3cm   of carcinoma   Core biopsy site changes present   LEFT BREAST  INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN   INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  is present as two foci  each 0 3cm in size  in 2  of 5 slides   No lymphovascular or perineural invasion are seen   No CIS is seen   Skeletal muscle is present and is free of carcinoma   Invasive carcinoma involves the inked inferior resection margin  over a 0 1cm  area with cautery on carcinoma  and is   0 1cm from the lateral resection  margin  The remaining margins are free    0 3cm   of carcinoma   CLINICAL DATA   History  A 41 year old woman   Operation  Left par