Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 34 CLINICAL DATA  Microcalcifications in left breast  status post radiation                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    REMOVED_DATE CM  MEASURE ON SLIDE D   GRADE 2 OF 3  PRESENT ON 7 OF 11 SECTIONS  EXTENDING TO A MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  NEGATIVE FOR LYMPHOVASCULAR INVASION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    INTERMEDIATE TO HIGH GRADE  ADJACENT TO AND ALSO AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  2 OF 11 SLIDES   HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  MICROCALCIFICATIONS WITHIN BENIGN BREAST TISSUE Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 19 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue as well as a needle localization wire  The fibroadipose tissue measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in aggregate  Each piece is inked and sectioned to reveal predominantly fibroadipose parenchyma  however there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm ill defined stellate firm area which abuts the inked resection margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A   I  and the area previously described is submitted in A and B  Gross Description by  RHONDA YANTISS  MD Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  SUSPICIOUS AREA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Gus John Vlahakes  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unknown.
