Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 52 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   ANTERIOR    BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST  RIGHT   POSTERIOR    BIOPSY  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FEW SMALL FOCI  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL DEEP TISSUE    BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 32                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 05     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  anterior breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast biopsy specimen which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm white gray  firm  stellate lesion grossly abutting the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and resubmitted in cassette G  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes A through F  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  posterior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  There are no areas suspicious for invasive carcinoma  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in cassettes H through L  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue  additional deep tissue   2  is a 3 x 2 x 1cm fragment of breast tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  No discrete lesions suspicious for invasive carcinoma are identified  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in cassettes M through Q  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST MASS POSTERIOR   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE  ADDITIONAL DEEP TISSUE  SPECIMEN  2   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   ANTERIOR BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   ANTERIOR   BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   POSTERIOR   BIOPSY PART C  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL DEEP TISSUE SPECIMEN   , Positive.
