ON_ID     Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE  Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   POSITIVE  3    NOTE  The patient presented with a right breast mass with peau d orange  appearance and erythema  On REMOVED_DATE  mammography showed a 2 4cm x 1 8cm  irregular mass at 12 00 with associated pleomorphic calcifications at the  medial and anterior spiculated margins of the mass  Extensive skin thickening  with fine linear calcifications were seen in the periareolar region  A core  needle biopsy showed a grade II III invasive ductal carcinoma  estrogen and  progesterone receptor negative and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu positive  3    BS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    04 16 09   Fine needle aspiration of a right axillary lymph node was positive  for malignant cells  BC 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   04 16 09    After neoadjuvant therapy  per clinic note  08 12 09   physical exam showed  resolution of right breast fullness and peau d orange and markedly diminished  erythema   Gross examination of the specimen revealed a 3 0cm x 3 0cm x 2 0cm  ill defined fibrous area with clip located at 12 00 consistent with tumor bed   On corresponding slides tumor bed is present with multiple scattered foci of  DCIS   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ve on immunostain performed  focal lymphovascular invasion within  the tumor bed  No residual invasive carcinoma is seen  Residual LVI is  additionally seen as scattered foci in nipple and skin dermal lymphatics and in  quadrants away from the tumor bed  The axillary contents were entirely  submitted for histological evaluation and it is difficult to identify  convincing residual encapsulated lymph node architecture following  chemotherapy  However foci of LVI are present  at least 8 discrete foci  mostly  in large vessels  up to 0 4cm   some with lymphoid aggregates around them  and  there is extensive tumor bed like fibrosis in adipose tissue suggestive of  prior metastatic carcinoma with extranodal extension  effe