Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Amend Addenda  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Breast  mastectomy with regional lymph nodes  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  ESTHER RHEI M D   CASE  BS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME              Addended Report              Resident  Marianna B Ruzinova  M D   Ph D   Jane E Brock  M B   B S   Ph D   Pathologist  Deborah A Dillon  M D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST  MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY LYMPH NODE DISSECTION S P NEOADJUVANT  CHEMOTHERAPY   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  moderately to poorly differentiated  modified  Bloom Richardson grade II III III  see NOTE    Extensive lymphovascular invasion is present  multiple foci  multiple blocks    No definite dermal lymphatic invasion is seen  see note    DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  solid and cribriform types  intermediate to high  nuclear grade   with focal calcifications  is present as a minor component  EIC  negative    Deep margin in negative for carcinoma  Skeletal muscle is present and shows no  involvement by carcinoma   METASTATIC CARCINOMA is present in eight of ten axillary lymph nodes  The  largest metastatic deposit measures 2 7cm  Extranodal extension is present   Seven of the eight positive lymph nodes show at least focal fibrosis compatible  with treatment effect   Note  The patient presented with an area of diffuse enhancement measuring 10cm  on MRI with masses in the axillary tail measuring 4cm and 3cm  Following  neoadjuvant chemotherapy  the area of diffuse enhancement measured 5cm on MRI   Gross examination revealed a 9 0cm ill defined area of nodular fibrosis as  well as two masses in the axilla measuring 2 7cm and 1 4cm  Microscopically   foci of residual invasive carcinoma are seen throughout all sections sampled  from the 9cm fibrous area and the two axillary masses are seen to represent  lymph node metastases  Histologic findings are compatible with a grade 3  response in the Miller Payne system   CLINICAL DATA   History  A 48 year old female with left breast cancer was on neoadjuvant   2 14 06 left breast skin biopsy negative   2 15 06 left axillary circumscribed mass core biopsy  DC  moderately  differentiated measures at least 1 2cm  no nodal tissue  ER PR positive     HER 2 neu neg    2 9 06 axillary FNA    malignant cells    Operation  Left MRM   Operative Findings  None given  Clinical Diagnosis  None given   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Left breast short suture   superior  long suture   lateral  bowtie on  axilla   B 2  Level I and II axillary contents   C 3  Level II palpable lymph nodes  ATTN  Breast Service S P neoadjuvant  chemotherapy   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh  in three parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s  name  unit number   Part A    1  Left breast   and consists of one modified radical mastectomy  weighing  REMOVED_CASE_ID  grams and measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm in overall dimension  with a pink tan skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 15 2cm  nipple measuring REMOVED_DATE x  1 0cm and everted and brown areola measuring REMOVED_DATE x 4 6cm  The deep margin is  intact and is inked black  The skin appears to be edematous and somewhat  granular  The specimen is sectioned  There are two white yellow firm tumor  nodules in the superior aspect of the axillary tail  The first nodule measures  2 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm and is surrounded by a darker tan rim of tissue up to 0 5cm  in greatest dimension consistent with lymph node tissue  The second nodule  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and is 1 1cm away from the first nodule  Two  additional lymph node candidates are found in the axillary tail   0 6cm and  0 5cm in diameter each   At REMOVED_DATE o clock of the mastectomy specimen  there is a  fibrous nodular area suspicious for malignancy  which is ill defined and  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The gross specimen is reviewed by Dr  Dillon of  breast pathology service   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First axillary nodule  9 frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Second axillary nodule  3 frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibroadipose tissue between the 2 axillary nodules  1 frag   RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area at the 11 o clock  10 frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple and representative sections of areolar skin  3  frags   RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin directly under the fibrous area at 11 o clock  2  frags   RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of edematous skin from 9 o clock   2 frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inner upper quadrant  1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inner lower quadrant  1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Outer upper quadrant  1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Outer lower quadrant  1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional axillary lymph node candidates  2 frags  ESS  Part B    2  Level I and II axillary contents   and consists of multiple   greater than 10  fragments of yellow tan lobulated fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE in aggregate  Four  4  lymph node candidates are  identified  the largest one measuring 0 7cm in greatest dimension   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lymph node candidates  4 frags  ESS   Part C    3  Level II palpable lymph nodes   and consists of three fragments of  yellow tan fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  One  1  lymph  node candidate is identified measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node candidate  bisected  2 frags  ESS   MRU mmm  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Deborah A