ctal carcinoma in situ adjacent to the invasive component raises the possibility that this is a new primary tumor rather than a true recurrence  although the latter possibilty cannot be excluded  Lymphatic invasion is identified  but it is not extensive  Added by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 02 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm right simple mastectomy specimen  with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm tan skin ellipse  There is an eccentric 2 3cm areola with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm firm  flattened  tan red nipple  There is a 2 3cm scar arising 0 4cm superolateral to the nipple  A black stitch designates the 12 o clock aspect  The resection margin is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 9 x 3 7cm region of dense gray white fibrosis with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm region of diffuse hemorrhage deep to the nipple which comes to 1 0cm of the superficial margin and 2 5cm of the deep margin  The remaining cut surface is 70  tan yellow lobular and 30  gray white fibrous tissue  No lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Hemorrhagic focus to nipple and deep margin B  Skin to hemorrhagic focus and superficial and deep margins C D  Hemorrhagic focus with surrounding fibrous tissue and skin E  Deep margin to hemorrhagic focus F G  Representative dense fibrous tissue away from hemorrhagic focus Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  LAN WANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Positive.
