Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY W REGIONAL LYMPH NODES  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  WELCH  WILLIAM  ROBERT  M D   DIAGNOSIS  by WELCH WILLIAM ROBERT M D   SPECIMEN LABELED  LEFT BREAST TISSUE    DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  intermediate nuclear grade  solid and mucinous  types  with MICROINVASION  the area of tumor  including microinvasion   is less than 0 1cm   Carcinoma is not present at the margin   No lymphatic vascular invasion   Healing surgical scar with fat necrosis  foreign body giant cell reaction   and polarizable foreign material   SPECIMEN LABELED  LEFT AXILLARY NODES    Nine  9  lymph nodes  no tumor present   CLINICAL DATA   History  None given   Operation  Modified radical mastectomy  Clinical Diagnosis  Left breast carcinoma  TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  Left breast tissue  2  Left axillary nodes  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by BOSENBERG MARCUS W  M D  PH D   The specimen is received fresh  in 2 parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s  name and unit number   Part 1   left breast tissue   is a 340 gram left modified radical mastectomy  specimen  16 x 11 x 3cm   with a white tan skin ellipse  9 x 2 5cm    The  specimen is received unoriented with a history of previous nodules in the upper  outer quadrant  The specimen will be oriented with a well healed 2 7cm scar  at the 12 o clock position relative to the nipple  which is 5cm away from the  scar  1 5cm deep to the scar is a firm  white red area  4 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm    containing a recent biopsy cavity  4 0 x 1 5cm   filled with organized red tan  clot  0 6cm from the deep margin with a smooth fascial plane without skeletal  muscle present  The wall of the cavity is firm and white yellow  ranging from  0 2 to 0 5cm in thickness  without gross tumor present  A second well healed  surgical scar  semi circular  2 5cm in length  is present in the periareolar  area  0 5cm from the unremarkable 0 5cm nipple  0 5cm deep to this scar is  a firm  white red area  3 x 2 x 1cm   containing a recent biopsy cavity  0 8cm  in diameter  filled with organized red tan clot  2 5cm from the deep margin   The remainder of the breast parenchyma is predominantly white and firm   Micro REMOVED_DATE   12 o clock biopsy cavity  RSS  4 f  4 c   Micro 5   deep margin of 12 o clock biopsy cavity  RSS  6 f  1 c   Micro REMOVED_DATE o clock biopsy cavity  skin with scar  RSS  1 f  1 c   Micro REMOVED_DATE   periareolar biopsy cavity  RSS  2 f  2 c   Micro 9   nipple and periareolar biopsy cavity  RSS  1 f  1 c   Micro 10   periareolar biopsy  skin with scar  RSS  1 f  1 c   Micro 11   deep margin of periareolar biopsy cavity  en face sections  RSS   3 f  1 c   Micro 12   upper outer quadrant  RSS  1 f  1 c   Micro 13   upper inner quadrant  RSS  1 f  1 c   Micro 14   lower outer quadrant  RSS  1 f  1 c   Micro 15   lower inner quadrant  RSS  1 f  1 c   Part 2   left axillary nodes   consists of multiple fragments of yellow fatty  tissue  measuring 4 x 4 x 4cm in aggregate  Nine possible tan lymph nodes  are found in the axillary tail  the largest measuring 2 0cm in greatest  dimensions   Micro REMOVED_DATE   9 possible lymph nodes and other  illegible  2 per cass   RSS  multiple frags  8 c   Reports to  HERGRUETER  CHARLES  A  M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST MASTECTOMY W REGIONAL LYMPH NODES   report_end  , Unknown.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 15 CLINICAL DATA  Nodule by mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemi